    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for August 15, 2026, centers on capitalizing against soft matchups, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.49) and **Drake Baldwin** (68.74) leading the charge as our most efficient starters. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable 4.37 xERA matchup and a significant +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage in the 4-hole. Simultaneously, **Drake Baldwin**\u2019s high score is buoyed by a strong 0.375 xwOBA trend and a positive park factor, making him a prime candidate for production against Ed Rodriguez. Both **Sam Antonacci** and **Heliot Ramos** also offer strong daily value; **Sam Antonacci** leverages a leadoff spot and a 7% platoon advantage, while **Heliot Ramos** remains a reliable start despite a slight platoon dip, sustained by the high-scoring potential against Fisher.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involves balancing aggressive SB-hunting with lineup efficiency. **Wade Meckler** (54.93) edged out several candidates due to his elite 19% SP skill advantage against Dobnak and a prime leadoff spot, effectively keeping him in the lineup despite his base projection being modest. Conversely, **Andy Pages** (46.78) remains a high-risk play today; his score is dragged down significantly by a brutal -19% SP skill penalty facing Misiorowski, who boasts a near-elite 2.03 xERA. While **Andy Pages** remains in the utility-OF mix, he represents the weakest link in today\u2019s configuration. We are closely monitoring **Nasim Nunez** (43.24) and **Gunnar Henderson** (42.45), both of whom are struggling against the pitching profile of I. Seymour; the -16% SP skill penalty for **Gunnar Henderson** specifically highlights the danger of holding him in a 5x5 Roto format when faced with high-caliber, low-ERA arms. \n\nFinally, our depth continues to be tested by health concerns, as **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, while **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** are absent from today's active lineups. We will continue to manage the remaining bench assets like **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Dominic Smith**, **Curtis Mead**, and **Luis Lara** to ensure we do not burn unnecessary game caps during these low-efficiency windows. With **Jackson Merrill** also facing a tough test against the quick delivery of Cantillo, we are prioritizing high-contact, high-speed situations to maintain our edge in the SB category.",
